1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,365
Can you draw this house
without lifting your pen?

2
00:00:02,415 --> 00:00:08,135
Trace it with your finger —
no line twice!

3
00:00:08,185 --> 00:00:10,905
If you start at the top…

4
00:00:10,955 --> 00:00:12,475
Oops, 3 lines left over!

5
00:00:12,525 --> 00:00:16,245
What if you start at the bottom-left corner?

6
00:00:16,295 --> 00:00:17,615
Success! The secret is where you start

7
00:00:17,665 --> 00:00:19,885
Count the lines that meet at each dot

8
00:00:19,935 --> 00:00:23,255
Only 2 dots have an odd number of lines —
start at one, finish at the other!

9
00:00:23,305 --> 00:00:25,775
At a dot you pass through, lines are used in pairs

10
00:00:25,825 --> 00:00:29,945
An odd dot has one line left over,
so it can only be the start or the finish

11
00:00:29,995 --> 00:00:34,465
So, can you draw this envelope?

12
00:00:34,515 --> 00:00:37,635
4 odd dots → impossible!

13
00:00:37,685 --> 00:00:39,905
The mathematician Euler found this rule
about 290 years ago

14
00:00:39,955 --> 00:00:42,055
Can you draw a star in one stroke?
Tell us in the comments!

15
00:00:42,105 --> 00:00:45,655
NEXT: What happens when you cut
a paper strip down the middle
